{"title":"Career roadmap · Vedic Teacher","role":"Vedic Teacher","summary":"A Vedic Teacher teaches Vedic literature, Sanskrit texts, Indian philosophy, Vedanta, Upanishadic thought, Vedic traditions and related knowledge systems. Depending on specialisation, the career may also involve Yoga philosophy, Jyotisha, Sanskrit, traditional pedagogy, research or cultural education.","facts":{"Starts":"Year 1","Current degree":"BA (Bachelor of Arts – General / Honours)","Course":"Vedic Studies / Indology / Yoga Philosophy / Jyotisha"},"about":[{"label":"Alignment","text":"Strong alignment"}],"intro":[{"type":"list","items":[{"text":"Formal school/college teaching positions may require additional teacher-training or postgraduate qualifications. Traditional institutions can have different eligibility and guru/acharya-based pathways."}]}],"horizons":[],"sections":[{"heading":"Typical route","kind":"other","blocks":[{"type":"flow","items":["BA Vedic Studies/Indology","Sanskrit/Textual Studies + Teaching Practice","Teaching Assistant / Vedic Studies Instructor","Vedic Teacher","Senior Vedic Teacher","Academic Coordinator / Acharya","Head of Vedic Studies / Research-Education Lead"]}]},{"heading":"Career horizons","kind":"horizons","blocks":[{"type":"table","header":["Period","Career focus"],"rows":[[{"text":"2026–2030"},{"text":"Build Sanskrit, Vedic texts, Indian philosophy, teaching methodology and research foundations."}],[{"text":"2030–2035"},{"text":"Specialise in Vedas, Upanishads, Vedanta, Yoga philosophy, Jyotisha, Sanskrit or Indian Knowledge Systems."}],[{"text":"2035–2040"},{"text":"Develop advanced teaching, curriculum, research and institutional leadership capabilities."}],[{"text":"2040–2046"},{"text":"Progress toward Senior Teacher, Acharya, Academic Head, Researcher, Curriculum Director or independent Vedic education specialist."}]]}]},{"heading":"What to build each year","kind":"build","blocks":[{"type":"table","header":["When","Build this","Learn from","Proof 